 "_doc": "Rooftop prop style for the 3D-to-pixel pipeline. Same light, bands, coverage, rim and outline rules as tools/art/common/enemy_style.json (one shared reduction: tools/art/samurai/pixelate.py process()). Ramps are darker than the characters' so dressing sits behind the actors at mid-dark value; the gunmetal, steel and cable ramps reuse the enemy palette. Emissive materials: r = red warning lights and sign letters, g = warm sodium door/lamp light, b = cyan/magenta neon and billboard panels. Material ids are written into the R channel of the id pass (id*10, max 25). Palette values are technical placeholders pending art-director sign-off. v2 (final polish): ramps lifted ~1.5x and cooled so props separate from the near-black near city layer under the dim global light; pack_props.py bakes a 1-px cool sky rim on top/left edges ('sky_rim') and scanlines the billboard panel ('panel_fx').",
